; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- user interface

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=The bookFido dialog: one check box for each library, the keys that work anywhere in it, and what happens after OK.
Setup=bookFido installed; the dialog open with Alt+Control+Shift+B.
Homework=Open the dialog, clear one library with its letter, then press Shift+F1 to hear its tip.

[step]

Say=One want: to choose which libraries to gather, and to know what happens next, before the browser opens.
Key=

[step]

Say=I press the desktop key for bookFido. Its opening dialog explains what will happen, and the focus is on the first library.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+B
Hear=bookFido dialog
Hear=Audible check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=There is one check box for each library, all checked to begin with. Each has an underlined letter, the first of its name.
Key=

[step]

Say=Audible is A.
Key=Alt+A
Hear=Audible check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Bookshare is B.
Key=Alt+B
Hear=Bookshare check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Goodreads is G.
Key=Alt+G
Hear=Goodreads check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Kindle is K.
Key=Alt+K
Hear=Kindle check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And NLS is N.
Key=Alt+N
Hear=NLS check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space clears a library you do not use, so bookFido skips it.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space again checks it.
Key=Space
Hear=checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tab moves through the boxes in order, and Shift plus Tab goes back.
Key=Shift+Tab
Hear=Kindle check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F1 says the tip for the box you are on.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=Kindle: every book on the same Amazon account
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F1 shows Help: each box with its tip, and the dialog's keys.
Key=F1
Hear=bookFido Help dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes Help and returns here.
Key=Escape
Hear=Kindle check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter, or Control plus Enter from any control, starts the run. Escape closes the dialog without gathering anything.
Key=Tab
Hear=OK button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=After OK, Edge opens. A library that needs you to sign in says so in a box; you sign in in Edge, then answer the box, and the run carries on.
Key=
Hear=Sign in to Audible in the Edge window, then press OK
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Each sign in is usually needed once, because bookFido keeps a browser profile of its own, separate from your everyday Edge.
Key=

[step]

Say=The rest is automatic. Progress is saved every couple of minutes, so a run can be cancelled and the next one continues where this one stopped.
Key=

[step]

Say=F11 checks for a newer version of bookFido, at any time in the dialog.
Key=F11
Hear=Checking for a newer version
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The dialog is the only window bookFido shows before Edge opens, so everything to decide is decided here.
Key=

[step]

Say=A library left unchecked is not visited at all: no page is opened and no sign in asked for, so a run can cover just one library when that is all you need.
Key=Alt+N
Hear=NLS check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Your choice of boxes can differ from run to run: Goodreads alone after finishing a book, all five once a month.
Key=

[step]

Say=That is the whole dialog: five libraries and a key for each. The next walk installs bookFido.
Key=
